  "pli-tv-bu-vb-ss9:2.3.52": "Sp 1.400: <i lang='pi' translate='no'>Sāṭakapattoti lohapattasadiso susaṇṭhāno succhavi siniddho bhamaravaṇṇo mattikāpatto vuccati</i>, “<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Sāṭakapatta</i>: what is meant is a ceramic bowl like an iron bowl, which is well-formed, has a nice and glossy surface, and has the color of a bee.” <a href='https://suttacentral.net/thig13.1/en/brahmali#1.1'>Thig 13.1:1.1</a>: <i lang='pi' translate='no'>Kāḷakā bhamaravaṇṇasādisā</i>, “Black like the color of a bee.” It seems plausible that this kind of bowl was made of the ceramic that is now known among archeologists as “Northern Black Polished Ware”. ",
  "pli-tv-bu-vb-ss9:2.3.53": "Sp 1.400: <i lang='pi' translate='no'>Sumbhakapattoti pakatimattikāpatto</i>, “<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Sumbhakapatta</i>: an ordinary ceramic bowl.” ",
